//! flags: -p canonicalize

// `count`, `avg` and `prod` are aggregation intrinsics (added alongside
// aggregate scans), and Parser::parse_identifier resolves a name against the
// builtin set before the enclosing scope. A binding of one of those names is
// therefore parsed as a call to the intrinsic and rejected, rather than
// shadowing it -- so those names are effectively reserved.
//
// This test pins that behaviour down: it used to be discovered by accident,
// as a parse error in unrelated tests whose layout happened to have a field
// called `count` (tests/bonsai/lower/trace.bonsai and friends, since renamed
// to `nCount`). The other half, that the names still work as intrinsics, is
// parsing/aggregation-names.bonsai.
func totals(xs : array[f32, 4]) -> f32 {
    count : mut f32 = 0.0;
    count += xs[0];
    return count;
}
